{
  "koral-function": 1,
  "purpose": "Culling",
  "description": "What of an indirect draw of entities is in sight, on the GPU: each instance's mesh box, placed by its matrix, tested against viewProjection, and what is in sight counted into its mesh's command — an IndirectDraws' in eGPU, whose commands start with no instances each frame — and its number written into visible, where the Draw's shader finds it (instances[visible[first + index]]). instances is the Draw's [entity(\"PER_INSTANCE\")] buffer, stride bytes an element with its MATRIX matrixOffset bytes in; ranges a MeshPack's rangeBuffer. How many instances there are is how many visible has room for: nothing of them is counted on the CPU. Given drawn, as big as instances, each element in sight is copied there where it is drawn too: a shader that reads its instance at first + index reads drawn as it is (what a batched Draw given cull does).",
  "tags": [
    "cull",
    "frustum",
    "in sight",
    "visibility",
    "gpu driven",
    "indirect",
    "instances"
  ],
  "graph": {
    "kgraph": 1,
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "instances",
        "type": "FunctionInput",
        "at": [
